{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>All who touch.</b> Rashi: 'Do I hear, whether worthy or not worthy?' etc. And one must wonder, for in that verse there is no mention of an olah offering. And one may say he relies on the olah of the daily offering in the preceding verse. And it seems to me that one need not force it so much, for in that verse it is written שנים ליום תמיד, and we know that the verse speaks of an olah, since it says in the passage of its offering שנים ליום עולה תמיד. And it is puzzling that in the passage of the daily offerings Rashi wrote: את הכבש אחד תעשה בבקר — even though it was already stated in the passage of ואתה תצוה, וזה אשר תעשה etc. — 'that was an admonition for the days of ordination, and this is a commandment for the generations.' And it seems to me that this 'for the generations' was needed for the other ordinations that they offered in the days of Ezra, just as in the days of Moses, and likewise for the future when it will be rebuilt speedily in our days. And further I say that this is the language of Rashi, for he stated 'that was an admonition for the days of ordination' without specification."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The comment quotes and engages with Rashi's interpretation on Exodus 29:37; דלק' appears to abbreviate דלקמן, 'below,' referring to the daily offering mentioned in the preceding verse (v. 38)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:21.847726741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}